Ques4: How does a quadcopter fly?
A quadcopter flies using 4 brushless motors and 4 propellers.
→ The propellers spin and produce ligt, which pushes the drone upward.
→ Gravity pulls the drone downward.
→ When lift is greater than gravity, the drone takes off.
→ Thrust is the force that moves the drone up, down, or forward.
→ Drag is the air resistance that slows down the drone.
→ Two propellers rotate clockwise (CW).
→ The other two rotate counter-clockwise (CCW).
→ CW and CCW rotation balance the drone and stop it from spinning.
→ The flight controller changes the speed of each motor to control movement.
→ By increasing or decreasing motor speed, the drone can take off, hover, move in different directions, and land.
